A||||5||MooCow||How to get reverse lights to work??||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||09-20-2001||01:33 AM||||I have an 87 GT but the tranny is from an 84 so it has the 4:10 gears.  Since I bought the car I have never had my reverse lights turn on and the bulbs are not burned out.  Any one know how I can get my reverse lights working again?&gt;<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||5
Z||000001||SLYGUY||09-20-2001||02:24 AM||||You are having the exact problem I am having. My bulbs are new, but I can't get it to work either. <P>The Haynes manual gives a very descriptive troubleshooting guide for it. Only problem is that you need a voltmeter. I'm gonna get one this weekend and see what's up.<P>Either way I think I will be replacing the backup light switch. You may need to do the same.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-20-2001||07:40 AM||||MooCow,<P>The 87 tranny had the switch in the transmission case. The 84 had a switch attached to the shifter. Your problem is you have no switch and no real place to mount one. You could get a shifter for a 4-speed trans and run the wires up to it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||09-20-2001||07:53 AM||||IRGuy is 100% correct, do just what he says.<P>Archie<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>MooCow,<P>The 87 tranny had the switch in the transmission case. The 84 had a switch attached to the shifter. Your problem is you have no switch and no real place to mount one. You could get a shifter for a 4-speed trans and run the wires up to it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||09-20-2001||10:13 AM||||Ken - If you make it down tomorrow I will show you on the 84 SE how the backup light switch is if you havent seen one before.  You'll probably find in your engine compartment somewhere dangling by the shift cables an empty wiring connector for the backuplight switch that would have been used in the getrag originally in that car.||||reg||1
